ca-06083-bos-matter-29456.title:
Consider recommendations regarding ratification of the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) 2026 Continuum of Care (CoC) Competition Consolidated Application, as follows:

a) Ratify the submission of the 2026 CoC Collaborative Application and related documents to HUD totaling $7,367,270.00 including recommended CoC community project applications, Community Services Department (CSD) project applications (collectively, the “CoC Projects”) for Fiscal Year (FY) 2026 HUD CoC Program Competition;

b) Authorize the CSD Director, or their designee, to take the following actions required for the application for, and acceptance of, HUD CoC Program competition funds awarded to the Santa Maria/Santa Barbara County CoC:

i) Execute FY 2026 CSD CoC Program grant agreements and related documents with HUD for the four CSD project applications that are part of the CoC Collaborative Application, in a form substantially similar to the previously approved and executed FY 2024-2025 CoC grant agreements, in the following estimated amounts, and all certifications, standard forms, and other related documents, subject to review and concurrence by Auditor-Controller and County Counsel including any reservation of rights the County may need to assert:

1) $191,944.00 for operation of the Homeless Management Information System (HMIS); 

2) $147,900.00 for operation of the Coordinated Entry System (CES);

3) $324,468.00 for Santa Maria/Santa Barbara County CoC Planning; and

4) $398,197.00 for renewal of the Youth Homeless Demonstration Program (YHDP) Permanent Supportive Housing (PSH) grant to extend this scattered site project grant;

ii) Authorize the CSD director to execute any other HUD CoC Program Competition related documents as required by HUD subject to review and concurrence by Auditor-Controller and County Counsel including any reservation of rights the County may need to assert; and

c) Determine that the above recommended actions are exempt from the California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA) per CEQA Guidelines Section 15378(b)(4) since the recommended actions are government fiscal activities which do not involve commitment to any specific project which may result in a potentially significant physical impact on the environment.

ca-06083-bos-matter-29458.title:
Consider recommendations regarding a Funding Agreement and related documents with Good Samaritan Shelter, Inc., 1114 South Broadway, Santa Maria, Fifth District, as follows: (4/5 Vote Required)

a) Approve and authorize the Chair to execute the Opioid Settlement Fund Program Agreement, providing a $200,000.00 grant to Good Samaritan Shelter, Inc. to provide qualified adult clients with recovery residence affordable housing at 1114 S. Broadway, Santa Maria, CA, APN 125-251-042; 

b) Approve and authorize the General Services Director to accept an Owner-executed Deed of Trust, Assignment of Rents, and Security Agreement, and an Owner-executed Promissory Note to secure the County’s $200,000.00 Opioid Settlement Funds Grant to Good Samaritan Shelter; 

c) Approve Budget Revision Request No. 1675 in the amount of $200,000.00 for appropriations funded by a release of restricted fund balance in the County Health Department Budget Fiscal Year 2026-2027; and

d) Determine that the recommended actions do not constitute a “Project” within the meaning of the California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA), pursuant to Section 15378(b)(5) of the CEQA Guidelines, because the actions consist of organizational and administrative activities of governments that will not result in direct or indirect physical changes in the environment.

ca-06083-bos-matter-29462.title:
Consider recommendations regarding Laguna County Sanitation District - authorization to use the Design Build delivery method and initiate procurement for the Electrical Upgrade Project; Fourth and Fifth Districts, as follows:

Acting as the Board of Directors, Laguna County Sanitation District:

a) Approve the use of the Design Build project delivery method for the Laguna County Sanitation District Electrical Upgrade Project, pursuant to Public Contract Code Sections 22160-22169;

b) Authorize the Public Works Director, or designee, to issue a Request for Qualifications to solicit Statements of Qualifications from prospective Design Build entities;

c) Authorize the Public Works Director, or designee, to evaluate Statements of Qualifications and establish a shortlist of the most qualified Design Build entities;

d) Authorize the Public Works Director, or designee, to issue a Request for Proposals to shortlisted Design Build entities;

e) Direct staff to return to the Board with a recommended Design Build entity and proposed contract award, including contract amount and contingency, upon completion of the solicitation process; and

f) Determine that solicitation for, and receipt of, Request for Qualifications and Request for Proposals is an administrative activity that will not result in environmental impacts and therefore does not constitute a “Project” within the meaning of the California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA) pursuant to 14 CCR Section 15378(b)(5).

