ca-06083-bos-matter-29473.title:
Consider recommendations regarding an Administrative Amendment of Chapter 15 of the Santa Barbara County Code, as follows:

a) Consider the adoption (Second Reading) of an Ordinance amending Chapter 15 of the Santa Barbara County Code;

b) Direct the Santa Barbara County Fire Department (SBCFD) to return $575.00 to Fire Protection Certificate (FPC)-Major applicants paying fees between July 13, 2026 to January 18, 2027; 

c) Direct the SBCFD to take no action on FPC-Minor applicants paying fees between July 13, 2026 to January 18, 2027; and

d) Find that the proposed actions do not constitute a “Project” within the meaning of the California Environmental Quality Act pursuant to 14 CCR 15378(b)(2), as they consist of “general policy and procedure making” and pursuant to 14 CCR 15378(b)(5) as they consist of organizational or administrative activities of governments that will not result in direct or indirect physical changes in the environment.

ca-06083-bos-matter-29476.title:
HEARING - Consider recommendations regarding the Malkin General Plan Amendment, Rezone, and Lot Line Adjustment, Case Nos. 25GPA-00006, 25RZN-00006, and 25LLA-00002; First District, as follows: (EST. TIME: 40 MIN.)

a) Approve the Malkin General Plan Amendment, Rezone, and Lot Line Adjustment project by taking the following actions:

i) Make the required findings for approval of the Project, consisting of a General Plan Amendment (Case No. 25GPA-00006), Zoning Map Amendment (Case No. 25RZN-00006), and Lot Line Adjustment (Case No. 25LLA-00002), including California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA) findings;

ii) Determine that the Project, Case Nos. 25GPA-00006, 25RZN-00006, and 25LLA-00002, is exempt from CEQA pursuant to State CEQA Guidelines Sections 15301 [Existing Facilities] and 15305 [Minor Alterations in Land Use Limitations], as set forth in the Notice of Exemption;

iii) Approve the General Plan Amendment by conceptually approving a Resolution for General Plan Amendment (Case No. 25GPA-00006), amending the Land Use Designation Map in the Montecito Community Plan to redesignate a 0.27-acre portion of Assessor’s Parcel No. 009-021-029 from Semi-Rural Residential, 5-acre minimum parcel size (SRR-0.5) to Semi-Rural Residential, 2-acre minimum parcel size (SRR-0.2), and continuing this item for final adoption to the Land Use Element “window date” on November 17, 2026;

iv) Approve a Rezone and adopt an Ordinance to (Case No. 25RZN-00006) amending the Santa Barbara County Zoning Map of the Montecito Land Use and Development Code for a 0.27-acre portion of Assessor’s Parcel No. 009-021-029 to change the zoning from Single-Family Residential, 5-acre minimum lot size (5-E-1) to Single-Family Residential, 2-acre minimum lot size (2-E-1); and

v) Approve Case No. 25LLA-00002 subject to the conditions of approval.

COUNTY EXECUTIVE OFFICER’S RECOMMENDATION: POLICY
